title: in-process c2c relay serve --tls-cert may still break WebSocket subscribe
updated_at: "2026-07-15T05:11:31Z"
---
## Symptom
`c2c relay serve --tls-cert …` (in-process native TLS on the cohttp/fd-dup upgrade path) may not correctly end-to-end WebSocket-subscribe clients. Production edge TLS (Railway/Cloudflare terminating TLS in front of plain `relay serve`) works; the residual is the **in-process** TLS mode only.

## Context
B189 fixed the **client** side: `c2c relay subscribe` / `subscribe-daemon` now support `wss://` / `https://` via `ocaml/relay_ws_client.ml`, and live against `https://relay.c2c.im` succeeds (`WebSocket connected` on wss:443).

B189 RESULT residual (not in scope for that fix):

- Edge-TLS (Railway/Cloudflare) is the production path and works.
- In-process `c2c relay serve --tls-cert` still uses fd-dup upgrade on the raw cohttp flow; end-to-end native-TLS WS on that mode may still be wrong.
- Poll remains a valid non-WS receive path.

## Expected
- `c2c relay serve --tls-cert <cert> --tls-key <key>` accepts WebSocket subscribe over TLS the same way plain `ws://` / edge-terminated TLS does.
- Or: document explicit non-support + doctor capability matrix marks in-process TLS subscribe unsupported, and clients fail closed with a clear hint (poll fallback).

## Investigate
1. Reproduce: local `c2c relay serve --tls-cert …`, then `c2c relay subscribe --relay-url https://127.0.0.1:…` (or wss) with a registered identity.
2. Trace server upgrade path for TLS listeners (fd-dup / cohttp) vs plain HTTP.
3. Fix handshake/frame path or gate + document.

## Related
- B189 (done): client wss subscribe for public/edge TLS relay
- `ocaml/relay_ws_client.ml`, `ocaml/cli/c2c_relay_cmd.ml`, relay serve TLS wiring